index 0000000000..c5cd5ec5d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/initiatives/agentic-professional-runtime/BRAINSTORM.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Bellow is a list of ideas, thoughts & stuff that I'm thinking about for the agentic-professional-runtime initiative.
+
+1. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) - use pulumi to manage infrastructure
+2. How does openclaw fold into this?
+3. How do we automate setting up individual workspaces?
+   - scenario: MacOS, Windows 
+   - scenario: Anthropic Native with Claude Desktop
+   - scenario: OpenAI Native with Codex App
+   - scenario: Hybrid with Claude Desktop and Codex App
+4. How do we automate setting up the organizational brain layer?
+5. In addition to an organizational layer aggregating data and metrics across all workspaces whether scoped to individual or team level what does it look like for every employee to have their own aggregation layer? Think openclaw, plus codex, plus claude desktop for the individual
+6. What does the flow look like for aggregating data across individuals without becoming a "big brother" or employee surveillance stack?
+7. What tools, 3rd party SaaS, and open source solutions can we leverage to build a privacy-preserving, employee-centric data aggregation layer?
+8. What is our strategy for dealing with Colorado Senate Bill 24-205 (SB24-205), also known as the Colorado Artificial Intelligence Act (CAIA)?
+9. For wealth management & legal how do we deal with privacy concerns and regulatory compliance (PII)?
+10. How do I test & QA the installer application when I have no MacOS?
+11. What does the installer flow look like? e.g Do we ask for example, "do you have an existing Claude Plan or ChatGPT plan?"
+12. What is a schema we can use that is interoperable between the SKILL's for codex, chatgpt, claude, are skills an Open Standard?
+13. 
